URL:          https://github.com/sacredbanana/astralbound

Astralbound
===========

An original space trading and combat game for the Commodore Amiga,
inspired by the scope and solid-polygon presentation of Frontier: Elite II.
This is a playable development prototype, with unfinished features and
performance still being tuned. It is not a finished Frontier-scale game.

Features
--------

- Explore a galaxy using an adapted HYG star catalog and generated worlds.
- Fly among moving stars, planets, moons, rings and orbital stations.
- Descend through weather to terrain, forests, cities and surface ports.
- Trade, mine, carry passengers, hire crew and take thirteen contract types.
- Visit station services, meet contacts and plan routes to job destinations.
- Buy ships and equipment, fight pirates and use lasers and missiles.
- Use autopilot, System Drive, time compression and portable commander saves.
- Choose ECS, AGA, indexed RTG or high-colour RTG graphics, with adjustable
  detail settings and a built-in performance test.
- Control flight and menus with keyboard, mouse, joystick or a CD32 pad.
- Watch an optional cinematic intro rendered by the game engine.

Requirements
------------

Kickstart/AmigaOS 3.0 or later and expansion RAM are required, including
on a 68000. The emulator-tested low-resolution ECS configuration has
2 MiB Chip RAM and 8 MiB Fast RAM; this is not a measured minimum.
Higher resolutions and detail settings need more memory and CPU speed.
An accelerator or fast emulator is recommended. Stock A500 performance
has not been established.

ECS and AGA support PAL and NTSC, including a 320 x 200 low-resolution
option. AGA needs an AGA machine and a 68020 or later executable.
RTG needs CyberGraphX V41+ or Picasso96's compatible CyberGraphX API,
and a suitable graphics mode. No SDL or OpenGL is required.

Select the executable for your CPU:

  Astralbound.000     68000 or later, no FPU required
  Astralbound.020     68020 or later, no FPU required
  Astralbound.030     68030 or later, no FPU required
  Astralbound.020fpu  68020/68030 with a 68881 or 68882
  Astralbound.040     Full 68040 with FPU
  Astralbound.060     Full 68060 with FPU

Use Astralbound.020 on an LC/EC040 or LC/EC060 without an FPU.

Installation and first flight
-----------------------------

Extract the archive to a hard disk, preserving its drawer structure.
Open Install with the system Installer V42.12 or later, or copy the whole
Astralbound drawer to your chosen destination. Existing commander saves
and graphics preferences are preserved by the installer.

Open the appropriate CPU icon or Play-AGA, Play-RTG or Play-RTG16.
The setup menu lets you choose graphics, resolution and detail before
starting. Low detail is the initial Amiga default. CLI example:

  Astralbound.020 --aga --lowres

The game allocates its required stack automatically for CLI launches.
Workbench icons request 256 KiB. Escape exits and restores the display.
At Haven, press L to launch and P for autopilot to the orbital Relay.
Read Astralbound.guide for controls, station services and flight advice.

Music is optional. Add your own supported ProTracker MOD files to the
music subdrawers; see music/README.txt. No music tracks are included.

